{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794173640,"nonce":"u0s6tG5OG18ced7LkDrGv+oIa2k=","message":"Built; where it differs from or adds to the design above:\n\n- **The rule's heading is in `doc/design/cli.md`**, under Aliases: \"The copy that reached the system first is canonical\", beside \"Any ID position accepts an alias\", since the alias is defined there. No aspect added. `doc/design/cli.md` \"A consolidated duplicate is drawn by its hash\" is renamed \"A duplicate is drawn by its hash\": it now holds before consolidation too. Every citation is repointed (only code cited it).\n- **The hook is wired explicitly, not by an `init()`**: `cache.RepoCacheIssue.SetReach(namespace, ReachFunc)`, and `commands/execenv` calls `jira.Register(backend)` where it opens the store (and in its test envs). The sync's own consolidation does not depend on that wiring: `firstToSync` calls `repo.Issues().FirstReached(jira.Reach, ids)`, the same rule with the hook passed in. Cache tests use a hook of their own and never import `jira`.\n- **The hook says which external issue a copy is linked to** (`cache.Reach{Issue, At, Rank}`): consolidation groups by `jira-id`, but an alias is matched by key, so alias resolution ranks copies only when every copy that reached the system is linked to one issue. A key moved or reused (two `jira-id`s) stays ambiguous.\n- **\"Cannot order\"**, since the Jira order is total among copies with contact facts: no carrier reached the system, the namespace has no hook, the reached copies are linked to two external issues, or the alias is carried in two namespaces. The error is an ErrMultipleMatch naming every carrier. A copy whose alias was set by hand (no `jira-id`, no `jira-create`, no marker) is never first, so it loses to the synced copy rather than making the key ambiguous; both docs say so.\n- **`jira-consolidated-into` moved from `cache` to `jira`** (`cache.ConsolidatedIntoMetadata` and `IssueExcerpt.Consolidated` are gone): alias resolution no longer reads it.\n- **`NewIndex` errors** on two copies of one `jira-id` neither of which has a contact, where it used to pick the lower id. The sync cannot write that state: a link is committed with a marker or after an attempt (`doc/design/jira.md` says so).\n- `cache/display.go` builds its index from one pass over the excerpts, as before, and calls the same `aliasNamed` as `ResolveAlias`; an alias two issues carry loads their entities, and no other does.","files":null}]}